ise fraction_unique) enabling exploration and letting the optimizer distinguish and improve candidates on the performance objective.", "validation_plan_suggested_by_judge": "In the next iteration check that per-dimension_std_mean > 0, mean_pairwise_distance > 0, fraction_unique increases (e.g., >0.1), and that objective scores show nonzero variance. If diversity returns but performance does not improve, consider adding a parameter_spread objective or adjusting exploration/exploitation balance.", "self_reported_confidence_uncalibrated": 0.85, "target_assessment": null}, "notes": [], "judge_raw_output": "The collapse looks like an optimizer / workflow issue: the population is identical (per-dimension std_mean = 0.0, mean_pairwise_distance = 0.0, fraction_unique = 0.031) while mutation_prob is at its lower bound (current = 0.0, default = 0.3). Re-enabling per-gene mutation is the simplest, low-risk change most likely to restore diversity quickly.\n\n<decision>\n{\n  \"failure_location\": \"optimization_workflow\",\n  \"root_cause_hypothesis\": \"The optimizer has per-gene mutation disabled (mutation_prob = 0.0 at its lower bound), so offspring cannot acquire per-parameter variation; this produced a collapsed population (per-dimension_std_mean = 0.0, mean_pairwise_distance = 0.0, fraction_unique = 0.031).\",\n  \"intervention_target\": \"optimization_workflow\",\n  \"rationale\": \"Run diagnostics show mutation_prob current = 0.0 (at lower bound) while diversity metrics are zero (per-dimension_std_mean = 0.0, mean_pairwise_distance = 0.0, fraction_unique = 0.031). Restoring mutation probability (to the default 0.3) will reintroduce per-gene random variation (with mutation_sigma = 0.08 already set) and is the most direct fix to break the degeneracy without changing objectives or scorers.\",\n  \"proposed_change\": {\n    \"params\": {\n      \"mutation_prob\": 0.3\n    }\n  },\n  \"expected_benefit\": \"Reintroducing mutation should increase per-parameter variation across candidates (increase per-dimension std and mean_pairwise_distance, raise fraction_unique) enabling exploration and letting the optimizer distinguish and improve candidates on the performance objective.\",\n  \"validation_plan\": \"In the next iteration check that per-dimension_std_mean > 0, mean_pairwise_distance > 0, fraction_unique increases (e.g., >0.1), and that objective scores show nonzero variance. If diversity returns but performance does not improve, consider adding a parameter_spread objective or adjusting exploration/exploitation balance.\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.85\n}\n</decision>", "change_id": "f7fa0ce08bb05ef9", "candidate_state": {"version": 0, "planner_guidance": null, "objective_ops": [], "implementation_patches": {}, "workflow_params": {"mutation_prob": 0.3}}, "validation": {"seeds": [3000, 3001], "use_planner": false, "candidate_objectives": ["performance", "distance_from_center"], "baseline_objectives": ["performance", "distance_from_center"], "baseline": [0.06513887923203086, 0.06513887923203086], "candidate": [0.3240528340108499, 0.29758271106224726], "baseline_mean": 0.06513887923203086, "candidate_mean": 0.3108177725365486, "delta": 0.2456788933045177, "min_improvement": 0.02, "candidate_constraint_violation": false, "details": {"baseline": [{"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 0.06513887923203086, "population_mean": 0.06513887923203086, "best": 0.06513887923203086, "n_invalid": 0}, {"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 0.06513887923203086, "population_mean": 0.06513887923203086, "best": 0.06513887923203086, "n_invalid": 0}], "candidate": [{"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 0.34124378989955084, "population_mean": 0.17504995245127633, "best": 0.3975908473388723, "n_invalid": 0}, {"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 0.31026963910462624, "population_mean": 0.143647704482641, "best": 0.3823686498403018, "n_invalid": 0}]}}, "outcome": "accepted", "re